      "estimated_minutes": 8,
      "reason": "The reviewer must distinguish uncertainty about which documents belong to the integrated whole from d01’s dispute over whether integration expands the agreement and forum-selection scope or merely bars parol evidence. The reference to 'what the parties may prove' requires a second look at how much of that incorporation-versus-evidence dispute the description names."
    },
    {
      "id": "a02",
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "score": 6,
      "estimated_minutes": 12,
      "reason": "The reviewer must verify the Proposal quotations and test the assertion that the disclaimer is 'aimed at' that document against the opinion’s treatment of the alleged advisory relationship. The remaining comparison is whether the claimed survival-or-extinguishment conflict names d01’s incorporation-versus-parol-evidence problem, rather than a separate dispute about the Proposal’s effect."
    },
    {
      "id": "a03",
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "score": 5,
      "estimated_minutes": 10,
      "reason": "The reviewer must check the claim about the named federal court and separate the subject-matter-jurisdiction objection from the mandatory-versus-permissive question. That comparison turns on whether the description’s asserted lack of exclusivity reaches d04’s construction of 'shall be brought,' despite bundling it with objections the court did not resolve."
    }
  ]
}
